    {
      "id": 477131,
      "username": "Priytesh",
      "name": "Priytesh",
      "created_at": "2025-08-12T06:28:09.159Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Voltass\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"151543\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/voltass/48/89391_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Voltass:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I am having a little problem on purchase invoice.</p>\n<p>I have a two VAT on one invoice 7% and 0% but after set it from tutorial about taxes on youtube from Frappe on submit get error \" Tax should be 7.0% of the base amount<br>\n<strong>Note:</strong> To correct base amount, fill in Tax Base Amount.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hi Voltass<br>\nPlease try the following either should work.<br>\nMethod 1: Use “Tax Category” per item</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to your taxable items (7%) in the invoice and set <strong>Item Tax Template</strong> with 7% VAT.</li>\n<li>For zero-rated items (0%), set <strong>Item Tax Template</strong> with 0% VAT.</li>\n<li>In the Taxes table, make sure <strong>Charge Type</strong> = “On Net Total” and <strong>Based On</strong> = “Item Tax Template”.</li>\n<li>Remove any extra “Tax Base Amount” you typed in — let ERPNext calculate it.</li>\n<li>Save &amp; Submit.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4><a name=\"p-477131-method-2-adjust-tax-base-amount-manually-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477131-method-2-adjust-tax-base-amount-manually-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>Method 2: Adjust “Tax Base Amount” manually</strong></h4>\n<p>If you want to keep both VATs in the same invoice without templates:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the Taxes table, for the 7% VAT row, set <strong>Tax Base Amount</strong> = sum of base amounts of only those items that are taxable at 7%.</li>\n<li>For the 0% VAT row, set <strong>Tax Base Amount</strong> = sum of base amounts of items that are zero-rated.</li>\n<li>Make sure <strong>Tax Amount</strong> is exactly <code>Base Amount × 7%</code> for the 7% row.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Extra checks</p>\n<p>Ensure <strong>“Validate Tax Amount”</strong> setting in your Purchase Invoice DocType isn’t too strict. If you want some tolerance, go to:<br>\nAccounts Settings → Tax Calculation Rounding</p>\n<p>and adjust.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check that <strong>Item Tax Template</strong> matches <strong>Purchase Taxes and Charges Template</strong>.</li>\n</ul>",
