    {
      "id": 477168,
      "username": "Priytesh",
      "name": "Priytesh",
      "created_at": "2025-08-12T09:47:14.249Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Right — in <strong>Frappe/ERPNext v15</strong>, the <em>“Based On”</em> and <em>“Tax Base Amount”</em> fields you’ve seen in older tutorials no longer appear in the default <strong>Purchase Taxes and Charges</strong> UI.</p>\n<p>ERPNext now automatically calculates the <strong>tax base amount</strong> from:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>items linked to the tax</strong> via <strong>Item Tax Template</strong></li>\n<li>The “Charge Type” and “Included In Print Rate” settings</li>\n<li>The “Applicable On” (Net Total / Valuation / Total) field</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So the fix for your <em>two VAT rates (7% &amp; 0%)</em> problem in v15 is a bit different than in older versions.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><a name=\"p-477168-how-to-do-it-in-erpnext-v15-without-tax-base-amount-field-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477168-how-to-do-it-in-erpnext-v15-without-tax-base-amount-field-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>How to do it in ERPNext v15 without Tax Base Amount field</strong></h2>\n<h3><a name=\"p-477168-h-1-create-two-item-tax-templates-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477168-h-1-create-two-item-tax-templates-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>1. Create two Item Tax Templates</strong></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to: <strong>Accounts → Item Tax Template → New</strong></li>\n<li>Name: <strong>VAT 7%</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Tax Type: VAT</li>\n<li>Tax Rate: 7.0</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Save.</li>\n<li>Create another template: <strong>VAT 0%</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Tax Type: VAT</li>\n<li>Tax Rate: 0.0</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-477168-h-2-assign-the-right-tax-template-to-items-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477168-h-2-assign-the-right-tax-template-to-items-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>2. Assign the right tax template to items</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Open each item in your Purchase Invoice and set the <strong>Item Tax Template</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li>Items with 7% VAT → VAT 7% template</li>\n<li>Items with 0% VAT → VAT 0% template</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-477168-h-3-set-up-purchase-taxes-and-charges-template-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477168-h-3-set-up-purchase-taxes-and-charges-template-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>3. Set up Purchase Taxes and Charges Template</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Go to: <strong>Accounts → Purchase Taxes and Charges Template → New</strong></li>\n<li>Add a row:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Type</strong>: On Net Total</li>\n<li><strong>Account Head</strong>: VAT Payable</li>\n<li><strong>Rate</strong>: 7.0</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Save.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>(You don’t need to add 0% VAT here; ERPNext will calculate it as zero based on the template.)</em></p>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-477168-h-4-use-the-template-in-your-purchase-invoice-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477168-h-4-use-the-template-in-your-purchase-invoice-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>4. Use the template in your Purchase Invoice</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>In the Purchase Invoice, select your <strong>Purchase Taxes and Charges Template</strong>.</li>\n<li>ERPNext will:\n<ul>\n<li>Apply 7% VAT to items with the 7% template.</li>\n<li>Apply 0% VAT to zero-rated items.</li>\n<li>Calculate correct <strong>tax base amounts</strong> automatically in the backend.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
